+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`: `Line.vat` used `unit_price * rate`, ignoring quantity; now `net * rate` (rule 3).
+- `billing/invoice.py`: `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for unknown rate names (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: `test_reduced_rate_small_item` expected VAT 0.02 / gross 0.52. PRICING.md rule 4 says 0.025 rounds to 0.03 (half up), so I changed the test to 0.03 / 0.53.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: all 6 tests pass (before: 4 failures).
+
+## Needs your attention
+- The test edit changes an expectation rather than the code. I followed the doc, which names the 0.025 -> 0.03 case. If finance actually wants 0.02, the doc is wrong, not the code. Please confirm.
+- Not verified: reconciliation against the accounting system. Floats passed as `unit_price` go through `Decimal(str())` as specified. `quantity` is not validated.
+- `docs/PRICING.md` untouched.
